;; Reviewed 2026-10-09 (written by Claude, from the design, the MACRO
;; manual, LLVM's code generator and the debugger runs; for the user's
;; review). Why this is right:
;; - Phase 16 step 3 (section 14, item 9): a REAL is an F_floating
;;   longword (.BLKF), a LONGREAL a G_floating quadword (.BLKG), in a
;;   register pair as a quadword is (Spilled's R0, R2 and R4).
;; - A constant is an immediate MACRO converts, rounding once as the VAX
;;   rounds: a numeral as written, its D made E (#0.1E0), a computed one
;;   as the shortest text of its value (1.0D0 / 4.0D0 is #2.5E-1), an
;;   integer as itself (#2 to DIVG3 is 2.0, checked on the guest). A REAL
;;   constant in a LONGREAL operation is widened by CVTFG at run time
;;   (CVTFG #1.25), as LLVM's fpext, so it keeps a REAL's precision.
;; - Arithmetic is ADDx, SUBx, MULx and DIVx at the wider of the two
;;   types, an integer converted by CVTWF, CVTWG or CVTLG ("/" of two
;;   integers is a REAL), a HUGEINT by POC_QTOG; a relation is CMPF or
;;   CMPG with the signed branches, since they set N and Z as for signed
;;   integers (MACRO 9.2.8.4, CMP). ABS is TSTx or MOVx, then MNEGx;
;;   LONG and SHORT are CVTFG and CVTGF.
;; - ENTIER checks its argument against -2^31 and 2^31 (trap 8), then
;;   CVTxL truncates and DECL makes the floor when converting back gives
;;   more than x, as LLVM's GenerateEntier does.
;; - A LONGREAL value parameter is passed as the address of a copy and
;;   copied again by the callee (Half), as a HUGEINT is; a REAL one as
;;   its longword (MOVF #1.5); a result comes back in R0, or R0 and R1
;;   (the calling standard). A LONGREAL waiting in R1 and R2 is moved to
;;   R4 and R5 before a call (MOVG R1, R4), as R0 and R1 are not kept.
;; - The debugger runs examine what each check computes, which RealsOut,
;;   built by both backends under -O2 and -OC, also prints, and tie, 22:
;;   2^53 + 1, a HUGEINT converted and a sum, is 2^53 + 2, a halfway case
;;   rounded away from zero (MACRO 9.2.8.3), where IEEE 754 rounds to
;;   even, 2^53. Then trap 8 at line 84, column 37, ENTIER, where LLVM's
;;   -trap-location gives it, and x / zero, the hardware's FLTDIV_F fault.
; VaxReals, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
